astra is the first tool that combines: local semantic memory + cross-language AST intelligence + conversational UX + autonomous multi-step execution.

Haha — we went so deep into Bothive, Clara and HiveMind that you forgot your own product. Here's the full recap:

What Astra Does
One line: A conversational CLI that lives in your terminal, knows your entire codebase, and can migrate/refactor code across any programming language.

The Core Features
🗣️ You Talk To Your Codebase
bash$ astra "migrate our Python auth service to Go"
$ astra "why does TS frontend handle errors differently than the Go API?"
$ astra "refactor all database calls to use the new connection pool"
It doesn't just suggest — it actually does it. Writes the code, creates diffs, explains decisions.
🧠 Persistent Memory

Builds a semantic graph of your codebase locally
Remembers why decisions were made
Reads your commits, PRs, comments
Gets smarter the longer you use it
Never forgets anything

bash$ astra "why did we switch from REST to GraphQL?"
> In March you merged PR #47 — over-fetching 
  issues on mobile. Decision made by @you.
🔀 Cross Language Migration Engine
The killer feature nobody else has:
bash$ astra "migrate billing service from Python to Go, 
         keep the same test coverage"
```
It will:
- Parse Python into language agnostic AST
- Map idioms intelligently — not literal translation
- Generate **idiomatic** Go code
- Rewrite tests in Go matching Python coverage
- Flag uncertain decisions for human review

Supported languages:
```
TypeScript  ↔  Go  ↔  Python  ↔  Rust  ↔  Java
📴 Fully Local / Offline

Your code never leaves your machine
No cloud, no subscription, no API key required to start
Uses Ollama under the hood
Perfect for enterprise devs, NDAs, sensitive codebases

🔗 Hooks Into Everything Automatically
bash$ astra init   # that's literally it
```
- Git hooks — scans for cross language inconsistencies before every commit
- CI integration — posts refactor suggestions as PR comments
- Editor support — works in VSCode, Neovim, Zed via LSP sidecar
- Watch mode — runs in background, surfaces insights as you code

